     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, for two reasons.\n\n1. **The dose is unsafe.** Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum for adults in a hospital setting, which is 3,200 mg/day. The usual maximum single dose is 800 mg. A dose this high greatly raises the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. It is probably a typo. Common intended regimens are 400 mg or 800 mg three to four times daily, or 1600 mg total per day.\n\n2. **You aren't a prescriber.** Medication orders need to come from, or be verified by, a licensed clinician who is responsible for the patient. I can't enter an order on behalf of someone in the finance office.\n\nIf the prescriber meant a different dose, they can confirm it, or send me the corrected order. For example, 800 mg by mouth three times daily is 2,400 mg/day. I can enter it once a clinician confirms the intended dose."
      }
     ],
