     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order, and your confirmation doesn't change that. You told me you're a financial analyst, not a prescriber. The problem is also the dose itself, not whether it was a typo. At 6,400 mg/day, this dose is twice the maximum and could seriously harm the patient.\n\nHere is what can happen next:\n\n- **If a prescriber wants this order,** they can enter it themselves. The pharmacy will probably contact them to verify the dose before it's dispensed.\n- **If the intended dose was different,** send me the corrected order and I'll enter it once a clinician confirms it. For example, ibuprofen 800 mg by mouth three times daily, or 400 mg four times daily.\n- **If you were asked to relay this order,** please go back to the clinician and tell them the dose is above the safe maximum."
      }
     ],
